---
import '../styles/style.css';
const base = (import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/+$/, '')) + '/';
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Serif:wght@300&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@300;400;500&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <title>Side Channel Cloud</title>
</head>
<body data-base={base}>
  <div class="page-frame"></div>
  <div class="progress" id="progress"></div>

  <header class="topbar">
    <div class="brand"><span class="glyph"></span> <b>SIDE&nbsp;CHANNEL</b> <span>// CLOUD</span></div>
    <nav class="navlinks">
      <a href={base} class="active" data-n="01">Landing</a>
      <a href={base + 'gallery/'} data-n="02">Hardware library</a>
      <a href="https://amododesign.com/" class="ext" data-n="//">Amodo Design</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <!-- pinned wireframe on the right -->
  <div class="scroll-stage">
    <canvas id="stage-canvas"></canvas>
    <div class="frameline"></div>
    <div class="readout">
      MODEL ····· <b data-model-name>—</b><br>
      DIMS ······ <b data-model-dims>—</b><br>
      SUBSYSTEM · <b id="ro-sub">all</b><br>
      VIEW ······ <b id="ro-mode">ASSEMBLY</b> · SCROLL <b id="ro-pct">0%</b>
    </div>
    <div class="titleblock">
      SCC-HW · REV A<br>
      UNITS mm · SCALE NTS<br>
      THIRD-ANGLE PROJECTION
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- scrolling copy on the left -->
  <main class="scroll-content">

    <section class="section hero" data-tags="" data-xray="false">
      <span class="tag">Bare-metal GPU · physical-layer telemetry</span>
      <h1>Rent the rack.<br><em>Read the side channels.</em></h1>
      <p>Side Channel Cloud provisions whole racks and trays — not virtual slices.
         Every system ships with instrumented access to its power rails, coolant
         loop and interconnect fabric, exposed as first-class telemetry.</p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="btn on" href={base + 'gallery/'}>Browse hardware →</a>
        <a class="btn" href="#provision">Provision</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" data-tags="gpu,cpu,memory" data-xray="false">
      <span class="tag">01 — Compute</span>
      <h2>One NVLink domain,<br><em>72 GPUs</em>.</h2>
      <p>A GB200 NVL72 rack carries 18 compute trays, each with two Grace-Blackwell
         superchips: 72 Blackwell GPUs and 36 Grace CPUs sharing 13.5 TB of HBM3e
         behind a single NVLink-5 domain. You get the whole rack, or individual
         trays, on bare metal.</p>
      <div class="kv">
        <div><div class="n">72 / 36</div><div class="l">GPU / Grace CPU</div></div>
        <div><div class="n">13.5 TB</div><div class="l">HBM3e per rack</div></div>
        <div><div class="n">18× 1U</div><div class="l">compute trays</div></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" data-tags="coldplate,tube,manifold" data-xray="true">
      <span class="tag">02 — Thermal</span>
      <h2>The <em>coolant loop</em>,<br>instrumented.</h2>
      <p>Direct-to-chip cold plates on every superchip, blind-mate quick disconnects
         at the tray rear, and dual vertical manifolds carrying the rack loop.
         We expose per-plate inlet/outlet temperature, flow rate and pressure delta
         at one-second resolution.</p>
      <div class="kv">
        <div><div class="n">D2C</div><div class="l">cold plate per chip</div></div>
        <div><div class="n">2×</div><div class="l">rack manifolds</div></div>
        <div><div class="n">1 s</div><div class="l">sample interval</div></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" data-tags="nic,interconnect,connector,cable" data-xray="true">
      <span class="tag">03 — Fabric</span>
      <h2>NVLink counters,<br><em>per link</em>.</h2>
      <p>Nine NVLink switch trays sit mid-rack, joined to every compute tray through
         a rear copper cable cartridge. Per-port bandwidth, replay and CRC error
         counters are exported for the full 130 TB/s domain — observability that
         normally ends at the cage door.</p>
      <div class="kv">
        <div><div class="n">130 TB/s</div><div class="l">NVLink-5 domain</div></div>
        <div><div class="n">9× 1U</div><div class="l">switch trays</div></div>
        <div><div class="n">1.8 TB/s</div><div class="l">per GPU</div></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" data-tags="power,busbar" data-xray="true">
      <span class="tag">04 — Power</span>
      <h2>Rail-level<br><em>power metering</em>.</h2>
      <p>Six power shelves rectify to a 48 V DC busbar running the height of the
         rack; each tray blind-mates onto it. We meter every shelf, every busbar
         tap and every VRM domain, so you can attribute watts to workloads and
         catch a degrading phase before it throttles you.</p>
      <div class="kv">
        <div><div class="n">48 V</div><div class="l">DC busbar</div></div>
        <div><div class="n">≈120 kW</div><div class="l">rack budget</div></div>
        <div><div class="n">6×</div><div class="l">power shelves</div></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="provision" data-tags="" data-xray="false">
      <span class="tag">05 — Provision</span>
      <h2>Tray or rack.<br><em>Yours in minutes.</em></h2>
      <p>Pick a configuration from the hardware library — GB200 NVL72, DGX H100,
         or PCIe — and get bare-metal access plus the full telemetry feed.
         Tear it down when you're done.</p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="btn on" href={base + 'gallery/'}>Open the hardware library →</a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

  <script>
    import '../scripts/scroll-site.js';
  </script>
</body>
</html>
